    tag: 'Flea & Tick',
    summary: 'A real-world account from PawGrade founder Kyle with his 75lb Lab mix Hershey: two ticks of different species were found on the bedsheets — not on Hershey — and both appeared unfed with no signs of having bitten. At the time, The Resistance was the only flea and tick product being used. No topical sprays, no essential oils, no chemical preventatives — just The Resistance added to food daily. This is exactly the mechanism The Resistance is designed to produce: it works from the inside out, altering the dog\'s body chemistry and scent at a cellular level so that ticks and fleas are repelled before they attach. The ticks were in the environment (carried in from outdoors) but chose not to attach to Hershey — they ended up on the bedsheets instead, unfed. Key points about The Resistance: it is a daily food supplement (1 tsp per day for most dogs) made from fermented nutritional yeast and B vitamins. It takes 4-6 weeks of consistent daily use to reach full effect as it needs to build up and alter body chemistry. It does not wash off in water — making it the only layer of protection that survives swimming, bathing, and rain. It works best as the foundation of a layered natural flea and tick protocol, combined with topical repellents (animalEO EVICT, rose geranium oil) and a metal flea comb after every outing. Finding ticks in the environment that did not attach to the dog is considered a positive result — it means the repellent is working. Two different tick species being present but unfed suggests broad-spectrum repellency, not species-specific. Important: even with The Resistance working, always do a thorough tick check after outdoor time — comb through fur, check ears, neck, armpits, groin, and between toes. Run a metal fine-tooth flea comb over white paper — flea dirt turns red/brown when wet. Q&A: Does The Resistance actually work for ticks? Real-world experience shows ticks present in the environment that did not attach to a dog using only The Resistance daily — both appeared unfed, suggesting the supplement successfully repelled them before attachment. How does The Resistance repel ticks? It works by altering the dog\'s body chemistry and scent from the inside out through fermented nutritional yeast and B vitamins — creating an internal environment that bugs find unattractive to land on. How long does The Resistance take to work? Full effect takes 4-6 weeks of consistent daily use. It needs to build up in the system to meaningfully alter body chemistry and scent. Is The Resistance enough on its own for tick prevention? It provides a strong foundation but works best layered with topical repellents like animalEO EVICT or rose geranium oil before outings, plus a flea comb check after every outing. What does it mean if ticks are found on bedsheets but not on the dog? It is a positive sign — ticks entered the environment but chose not to attach to the dog, which is the intended outcome of a repellent working correctly.',
